    "result_text": "Done. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec requires `checkDigit` \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode` \u2014 on the owner response. I followed the codebase's established pattern for derived read-only owner fields (like `membershipNumber`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139, read-only) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct auto-maps it by name.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getCheckDigit()` getter that computes the Luhn check digit over the digits in `customerCode`, mirroring the exact algorithm the acceptance test uses (null-safe, non-digits skipped, `(10 - sum%10) % 10`).\n\nNo OfficeFloor YAML or function changes were needed: the existing `RespondWithOwner` \u2192 `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` boundary serializes the new derived getter automatically, so every response path (`GET`, `POST`, `PUT`) carries `checkDigit`.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
