        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the established conventions in `Owner` cleanly:\n\n- The entity already hosts a family of `@Transient` derived getters \u2014 `getDisplayName`, `getInitials`, `getMembershipNumber`, `getMembershipLevel`, `getLocality`, `getContactPreference`. Adding `getCheckDigit` as another `@Transient` derived-from-`customerCode` property is additive and consistent, not a new concern grafted onto the class.\n- It's placed directly after `getMembershipNumber`, so the two getters derived from `customerCode` sit together \u2014 natural grouping.\n- The Javadoc matches the house style of the neighbouring getters exactly (purpose line + \"Not persisted \u2014 derived from {@link ...}\"), and the OpenAPI `checkDigit` schema mirrors the adjacent `membershipNumber`/`customerCode` entries (title/description/`readOnly: true`).\n- The inline computation length is in line with the existing `getMembershipLevel`, which also keeps a multi-line derivation inline; there's no established util class to extract to, so inlining follows the codebase's own convention rather than fighting it. No duplication is introduced.\n\nThe entity is not becoming a catch-all \u2014 it's the deliberately chosen home for these derived read-only properties, and this follows that pattern."
